                <description><![CDATA[<article>
				<blockquote class="messageText SelectQuoteContainer ugc baseHtml">
					
					<img src="https://i.discogs.com/efFr9-tSQl25MJv1K2zc_XyjY7IjPl-Ge9NcyH3iXIs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTEyNzkw/MzUzLTE2NzM2Mzg2/MjYtOTk0My5qcGVn.jpeg" class="bbCodeImage LbImage" alt="[​IMG]" data-url="https://i.discogs.com/efFr9-tSQl25MJv1K2zc_XyjY7IjPl-Ge9NcyH3iXIs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTEyNzkw/MzUzLTE2NzM2Mzg2/MjYtOTk0My5qcGVn.jpeg" style=""> <br>
<b><i>Duas Caras</i> (English: <i>Two Faces</i>) is a Brazilian telenovela produced and broadcast by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TV_Globo" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">TV Globo</a> from 1 October 2007 to 31 May 2008. It is created by Aguinaldo Silva and directed by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolf_Maya" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Wolf Maya</a>. Starring <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dalton_Vigh" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Dalton Vigh</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marjorie_Estiano" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Marjorie Estiano</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alinne_Moraes" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Alinne Moraes</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C3%A9bora_Falabella" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Débora Falabella</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A1zaro_Ramos" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Lázaro Ramos</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let%C3%ADcia_Spiller" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Letícia Spiller</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betty_Faria" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Betty Faria</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fl%C3%A1via_Alessandra" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Flávia Alessandra</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renata_Sorrah" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Renata Sorrah</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suzana_Vieira" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Suzana Vieira</a>, and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ant%C3%B4nio_Fagundes" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Antônio Fagundes</a>.<br>
It is the first telenovela by Rede Globo to be produced in <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HDTV" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">high-definition</a>.<br>
<br>
The telenovela spans through Maria Paula's revenge against Marconi Ferraço, her ex-husband that robbed her of all her inheritance.<br>
<br>
The album containis English songs from international artists that are part of the soundtrack:</b><br>
<br>
<ol>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_One_(Alicia_Keys_song)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">No One</a> - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alicia_Keys" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Alicia Keys</a></li>
<li>Let Me Out - Ben's Brother (Music theme of Benoliel)</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Same_Mistake" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Same Mistake</a> - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Blunt" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">James Blunt</a> (Music theme of Maria Paula and Ferraço)</li>
<li>Scared - Tiago Lorc (Music theme of Sílvia and Ferraço)</li>
<li>Lost Without You - Robin Thicke (Music theme of Sílvia)</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss_Kiss_(Chris_Brown_song)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Kiss Kiss</a> - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Brown_(American_singer)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Chris Brown</a> feat. <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T-Pain" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">T-Pain</a> (Music theme of Zidane e Gyslaine)</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/So_Much_for_You" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">So Much for You</a> - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashley_Tisdale" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Ashley Tisdale</a> (Music theme of Alzira)</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gimme_More" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Gimme More</a> - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Britney_Spears" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Britney Spears</a> (Music theme of Texas Bar)</li>
<li>2 Hearts - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kylie_Minogue" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Kylie Minogue</a> (Music theme of Débora)</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/How_Deep_Is_Your_Love_(Bee_Gees_song)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">How Deep Is Your Love</a> - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bird_and_the_Bee" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">The Bird and the Bee</a> (Music theme of Dália, Bernadinho e Heraldo)</li>
<li>You Are So Beautiful - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ivo_Pessoa&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Ivo Pessoa</a> (Music theme of Júlia and Evilásio)</li>
